course: dictionary
lesson: 12162
title: Component: one part of something bigger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A component is one of the parts that something is made of. Look at the words around it for clues. «The bike has three main components: the frame, the wheels and the brakes.» The list tells you the components are parts, and the bike is the whole thing they make up.
explain: Components can be parts of a machine, a system or a circuit. «A circuit needs a battery, a bulb and a switch to work.» Each of these is a component of the circuit. A quick check: swap in the word part. Does «each of these is a part of the circuit» still make sense? Then your meaning is right.
explain: Maths uses the word too. «A vector has two components, one across and one up.» Here the components are the separate parts that add together to make the whole vector. Context is what tells you which meaning is being used.
fact: A component is one of the parts that something is made of.
fact: In science, a component of a circuit is a part such as a bulb, battery, wire or switch.
fact: In maths, the components of something are its separate parts that together make up the whole.
fact: A key component is a very important part.
fact: «Component parts» means the separate parts that together make something.
exercise: «The bike has three main components: the frame, the wheels and the brakes.» What is a component? | A road with lots of hills | The rider | A bell that rings when you cycle | *One of the parts that something is made of
exercise: Which of these is a component of a circuit? | *A bulb | A cloud | A cupboard | A football
exercise: «A healthy diet has several components, like fruit, vegetables and protein.» What are the components in this sentence? | Foods that taste nice | Places where you buy food | Rules for eating | *Parts that together make up a healthy diet
test: «The vector has two components, one across and one up.» What are the components of a vector? | *Parts that together make up the vector | The numbers on a clock | A map of the playground | Arrows that point at the sky
test: Which phrase means a very important part? | *Key component | Long walk | Sleepy cat | Blank page
exam: Mia says a component is a kind of cake. What does component really mean? | A cake with icing | A map of a city | A type of animal | *One of the parts that something is made of
